{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund a 30-35 Railcard",
        "additional_details": "We think the 26\u201330 Railcard leaves a gap for individuals aged 30 to 35 who may be navigating rising living costs, rent increases, and commuting expenses. Those in their early 30s must pay full price despite often being at critical early stages in their careers or starting families.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to fund a railcard for adults aged 30-35.",
